/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harudagondi/bevy_oddio/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harudagondi/bevy_oddio/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harudagondi/bevy_oddio/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harudagondi/bevy_oddio/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harudagondi/bevy_oddio/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harudagondi/bevy_oddio/deployments","created_at":"2022-07-24T16:30:21Z","updated_at":"2025-11-24T01:47:33Z","pushed_at":"2023-11-06T00:59:02Z","git_url":"git://github.com/harudagondi/bevy_oddio.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:harudagondi/bevy_oddio.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/harudagondi/bevy_oddio.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/harudagondi/bevy_oddio","homepage":null,"size":98,"stargazers_count":39,"watchers_count":39,"language":"Rust","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":5,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":25,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":5,"open_issues":25,"watchers":39,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Currently, `bevy_oddio`'s frames are hard-coded as `[f32; 2]`. This is fine when audio files and signals are stereo, however this does not work when they are mono or on multiple channels.\r\n\r\nThere are multiple ways to deal with this:\r\n\r\n(1) Make `Audio` and `AudioSource` generic over type `F`, where `F` implements `oddio::Frame`.\r\n(2) Create multiple structs of `Audio` and `AudioSource` for each number of channels, possibly up to a limit.\r\n(3) Make `F` actually a boxed dyn trait.\r\n(4) Make `Audio` a visitor pattern. This does not solve `AudioSource`.\r\n(5) Make `Audio` and `AudioSource` a trait that is implemented for an inner generic `Audio`\r\n\r\nHere are some issues with each approach.\r\n\r\n- (1) and (4) is blocked by bevyengine/bevy#5432.\r\n- (2) probably needs a proc-macro. Also limited by number of channels we implement.\r\n- (3) either needs `Box` (which is not Send), or Arc<Mutex> (which locks whoops). Also, due to orphan rule, that boxed trait must be newtyped.\r\n- (4) is like (2) where it is limited by the number of channels we implement.\r\n- (5) needs trait resources (which doesn't make sense?) or trait queries (very debated in the bevy discord whether or not it should be added.\r\n- (1) should be solved when support for variadics in rust exist.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harudagondi/bevy_oddio/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harudagondi/bevy_oddio/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/1215600807","html_url":"https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/issues/5432#issuecomment-1215600807","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/5432","id":1215600807,"node_id":"IC_kwDODf6-U85IdJin","user":{"login":"NathanSWard","id":43621845,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNjIxODQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43621845?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanSWard","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanSWard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanSWard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanSWard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanSWard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanSWard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanSWard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanSWard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanSWard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanSWard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanSWard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-15T18:43:37Z","updated_at":"2022-08-15T18:55:26Z","body":"~~IIUC, this is correct behavior?\r\nEach Asset requires a unique `uuid` in order for the asset server to distinguish between types.\r\nHowever, a generic type is simply a template. So each instantiation of the generic e.g. `Foo<i32>` or `Foo<String>` for example, would each need their own UUID.~~\r\n\r\nAhh, nvm, generic support for TypeUuid was added 👍 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/1215600807/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"NathanSWard","id":43621845,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNjIxODQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43621845?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanSWard","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanSWard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanSWard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanSWard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanSWard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanSWard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanSWard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanSWard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/user